    "title": "CBS cancels some fan-favorite shows for 2026-27 schedule",
    "text": "EntertainmentThe network is saying goodbye to these shows. APBy EmilyAnn Jackman | ejackman@pennlive.comIf you’re a fan of the CBS network and its programming lineup, you might be disappointed to know that a few of its shows have ended up on the chopping block for the 2026-2027 season. In fact, some will be disheartened to find out that two fan favorites have ended up by the wayside. On Friday, CBS announced the cancellation of “Watson” after two seasons and “DMV” following its only season. The two shows are scheduled to air their season finales on May 3 and 11, according to The Hollywood Reporter. The cancellations were announced ahead of the network’s 2026-2027 schedule reveal on April 15.For those who aren’t aware of “Watson,” the show follows Dr. John Watson, played by Morris Chestnut, who solves medical mysteries at a clinic for rare disorders after the death of his friend, Sherlock Holmes. Meanwhile, “DMV” followed Harriet Dyer, Tim Meadows, and Tony Cavalero as underpaid employees going through workplace and personal drama at an East Hollywood DMV. These latest cancellations follow the news that CBS comedy “The Neighborhood” will end its run with the current eighth season.The show’s season finale will air on May 11 and is titled, “Welcome to Goodbye.”Popular convenience store chain plans to spend nearly $1 billion on 100 storesBeloved retail chain closes 92 stores in global shift from mallsBishop T.D. Jakes’ daughter narrowly avoids paralysis after fall. Here’s what to knowEmilyAnn Jackman is a trending reporter for Penn Live. She handles the top trending topics on social media, as well as breaking stories in pop culture and entertainment news that goes viral on a national...",
